<title>USA: Kansas feedlot cattle trade quiet, no sales - USDA.</title>
<headline>Kansas feedlot cattle trade quiet, no sales - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DODGE CITY 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade was quiet, with no sales slaughter steers or heifers confirmed, USDA said.</p>
<p>Inquiry and demand was moderate. Feedlots extremely current. Sales confirmed this week on 108,400 head including 21,700 head or about 20 percent previously contracted or formulated cattle.</p>
<p>Confirmed - none</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
